# Routing development attempt 1 (preserved)

This separately frozen development attempt exercised real IPA analysis, fixed-grammar CEGIS and native `route_model` consumption. Two computed repairs passed separate Docker execution oracles with zero provider calls. The two functional cases produced actual neural-residual routing decisions.

All six model cells were prevented from dispatch because the existing primary credential had expired on 2026-09-13. No HTTP POST occurred, no response usage exists, and no baseline/residual quality or comparative token saving was measured. `summary.json`'s `complete` means that all eight cells have terminal records; it does not mean the scientific comparison completed. The nominal 0/4 baseline and 2/4 system successes include unavailable transport cells and must not be presented as a quality comparison.

`oracle_sensitivity.json` verifies that both public and separate audit validators reject the four original programs. This supports test sensitivity, not general coverage. Internal CEGIS proof gates are marker/hash controls; no native SMT proof was counted. The native router received `available_proofs=0`, and its bounded behavioral obligation was discharged only by public execution checks.

The local-only preflight computed both supported repairs before the full run (a development deviation from the interleaved cell order); no model call occurred in either stage. After the root agent refreshed the existing primary credential through the ordinary Grok CLI, an identical fresh generation was frozen in `../routing_v2/`. This directory's effects and outcomes remain unchanged. Its call IDs were not silently retried.
